/*
  Immunization Chat Bot — SRS v2.0 aligned prototype
  Content & formulas sourced from: Immunization in Practice (IIP) Participant Manual,
  MoH Ethiopia, Sept 2023 — Chapter 2 (Vaccine & Cold Chain Management).

  Key correctness notes (per manual):
  - Forecasting (Target population): Annual need = Target pop * Coverage * doses/individual * Wastage Factor
    Wastage Factor = 100 / (100 - wastage rate%)
    25% buffer stock is a SEPARATE stock-management concept (assumed available at facility),
    NOT multiplied again into the forecast — shown as an informational add-on.
    AD Syringe formula mirrors the vaccine-need formula (1 AD syringe per dose).
    Mixing syringe = Number of Vials * Wastage Factor — ONLY applies to reconstituted vaccines
    (BCG & Measles in Ethiopia).
    Number of Vials = total doses / doses per vial.
    Safety box = (Total AD Syringe + Total Mixing Syringe) * Wastage Factor / 100.
  - Consumption method: Need = (Beginning Balance + Received) - (Ending Balance + Wasted unopened doses)
  - Session method: Annual need = posts * weeks * sessions/week * avg vials/session * doses/vial
  - Stock levels: Safety stock = supply-period need * 25%
      Minimum stock = Safety stock + Lead time consumption (Lead time consumption = supply-period need / 4)
      Maximum stock = supply-period need + Safety stock
  - Wastage: VUR% = doses administered / (Begin + Received - End) * 100 ; VWR% = 100 - VUR
      Wastage Factor = 100 / (100 - VWR)
  - MDVP: opened multi-dose vial may be kept up to 28 days if ALL criteria met (WHO-prequalified,
    approved for 28-day use, not expired, stored 2-8C, VVM not at discard point, not frozen).
    Ethiopia applies MDVP to bOPV, IPV, Td, PCV-13. Reconstituted BCG & Measles: discard within 6 hrs
    of opening or end of session, whichever first — MDVP does NOT apply to them.
  - VVM: Stage 1 & 2 = safe to use; Stage 3 & 4 = discard (central square same/darker than outer circle).
  - Shake test: compare suspect vial vs. a known-frozen control vial; if suspect sediments at the
    SAME rate or FASTER than control => was frozen => discard. Slower sedimentation => safe to use.
*/

